On Tuesday 23 March 2004 13:32, John Cowan wrote:
> xahlee.org scripsit:
> > does anyone has an example? is the word also mean category as in animal
> > classification?
>
> No, "jutsi" does that job.

"jutsi" doesn't necessarily refer to animal classification or to any rank 
within a classification system; e.g. le'i la'orseldze cu jutsi le'i 
xinjoiropno. "lanzu" could also refer to a language family, or families of 
other things. The term for "family" as a level of Linnean taxonomy is 
"lazyjutsi".

